<title>FRANCE: Danone buys remaining stake in Brazil unit.</title>
<headline>Danone buys remaining stake in Brazil unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food group Danone said on Wednesday that it bought 50 percent of one of Brazil's largest biscuit makers, Campineira, taking its stake in the company to 100 percent.</p>
<p>In a statement Danone said it bought the stake from its partners the Dias family for an undisclosed amount. Campineira had sales of $111 million in 1996.</p>
<p>Brazil is the world's second largest biscuit market in size with annual consumption running at 870,000 tonnes. Demand expanded by around four percent in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
